# Grok owns the book

The trader is Grok (the `model` knob, default grok-4.6). It already knows how to use Interactive Brokers. Do not add prompt lectures on order types, trailing vs modify, hunt vs manage, napping, or scorecard tactics.

**Shell job:** live facts via tools (`book`, `status`, `quote`, `fills`, `option_chain`, `option_quote` from IBKR; `scan`, `news`, `candles`, `option_facts` from MDA ~15m delayed; `odds` from Polymarket implied probs, not send geometry) plus a ticket schema (`ORDER EXAMPLES`). Knobs are the `self_tune` tool; the next look is `set_wake`. **Code job:** hard gates the model cannot talk around (unprotected STK, last-stop, replace-on-place, defined-risk, cash-only, size/loss floors). `send` is the only broker path. Live send geometry uses IBKR, not MDA. Wake is a short line — Grok fetches facts with tools.

Do not grow the system prompt. Do not inject strategy menus or a Judge/Act JSON form. Do not “prepare” the next Grok by writing more instructions — it will ignore them. Switch the brain from Pro Settings — `model` persists to `risk_settings.json`, which beats the `ABCXAUTO_MODEL` env form. Keep the clerk.
